Package: dvbrx
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: BILLY Rémi <byhoster.association@gmail.com>
Section: video
Priority: optional
Depends: dkms, kmod, passwd, @DEPENDS@
Recommends: @RECOMMENDS@
Suggests: dvbrx-web, uhd-host, tvheadend, dvb-tools
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Homepage: https://github.com/TrusterBSW/DVB-Rx
Description: real-time DVB receiver on software radios, seen as a /dev/dvb tuner
 dvbrx demodulates and decodes digital television in real time from a
 software radio (USRP B210, bladeRF 2.0 micro, HackRF One): DVB-S, DVB-S2 and
 DVB-S2X up to 256APSK, DVB-C, DVB-T and DVB-T2. A kernel module (DKMS) exposes
 each radio as a standard Linux DVB adapter (/dev/dvb/adapterN), so tvheadend,
 VLC or dvbv5-zap use it like a hardware tuner; LNB control through an ESP32.
 .
 The radio libraries (libuhd, libbladeRF, libhackrf) are loaded at run time:
 only those of the radios in use are needed. The kernel module is built for
 the running kernel and needs its headers.
